<title>FRANCE: MOTOR RACING-PANIS LEAVES HOSPITAL.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-PANIS LEAVES HOSPITAL.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Formula One driver Olivier Panis has left hospital in Montreal following his crash in the Canadian Grand Prix 10 days ago, the Prost team said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Panis, who suffered multiple fractures to  both legs when his Prost-Honda crashed into a barrier, left hospital on Monday and flew to France to continue his convalesence in Brittany.</p>
<p>Prost has named Italian Jarno Trulli, who has been competing in F1 for Minardi this season, as Panis's replacement for the French Grand Prix at Magny Cours on Sunday.</p>
